      },
      "message": "fix(sinker): Sinker Burn and Sinker Side Burn take a start and an exit pick\n\nA Sinker Burn reads a pick as an angle round its burn position. The\nstart pick is where the orbit starts; the exit pick is where the orbit\nends before it returns to the burn position and retracts. A circle keeps\nits own vertices and makes one full turn; a vector orbit keeps its\ndirections and changes the order only. A Sinker Side Burn reads a pick\nas an end of its side move: the burn position or the wall end.\n\nAn impossible pick is refused by name at the command door and at\ngeneration: a pick without an orbit, a pick on the burn position, a\npick on no vector, an exit that the vector order cannot end on, a side\nburn pick at the middle of the move. With no pick each generator calls\nthe earlier function, so every existing path is identical.\n\nThe Geometry tab of each kind has typed Start point and Exit point\ngroups. MCP edit_operation sets the picks through the shared field.\n\nFixes #3333\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
